==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|án}}, {{m|non|ón}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*ēnu}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈauːn/}}
* {{rhymes|is|auːn|s=1}}
* {{IPA|is|/ˈaun/}} (when forming a phonetic unit with an unaccented pronoun, e.g. {{m|is||án þess|without it}}: {{IPA|is|/ˈaun.ðɛs/}})

===Preposition===
{{head|is|preposition}}

# {{lb|is|with genitive}} [[without]]
#* ''[[nenna#Icelandic|Nennirðu]] að [[koma#Icelandic|koma]] [[með#Icelandic|með]] [[ég#Icelandic|mér]] '''án''' [[leiðindi#Icelandic|leiðinda]]?''
#*: (lit. [are you bothered with] to come with me '''without''' trouble?)
#*: Would you [[mind]] [[coming]] [[with]] [[me]] '''without''' any [[trouble]]?

===Anagrams===
* {{l|is|ná}}

